cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use proctor in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "proctor: the exam proctor for AI coding agents"
abstract: >-
  proctor checks whether an AI coding agent did the work or gamed its own
  evaluation. It detects evaluation tampering in code changes (skipped, deleted
  or weakened tests, rigged test harnesses, answer-key special-casing) with
  deterministic rules; measures generalization to held-out tests the agent never
  saw; benchmarks coding agents on tasks mined from a repository's own bug-fix
  history; and checks refactors for behavior changes by differential execution.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Naveen Babu
    family-names: Narayanan Nair
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1425-498X"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-24
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nbn07/proctor"
url: "https://github.com/nbn07/proctor"
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - reward hacking
  - software testing
  - test integrity
  - held-out evaluation
  - benchmark
  - differential testing
  - large language models
